  "note": "Covers both the Linear web app and the Windows/Mac desktop app (same keymap per Linear's own docs). The full shortcut list otherwise lives only behind Linear's in-app '?' help overlay (not a fetchable doc page), so this is assembled from every linear.app/docs page that documents shortcuts plus keycombiner.com/collections/linear (cross-checked entry by entry against the official pages; used only where it did not conflict with an official page). Left out rather than guessed: 'Archive issue' and 'Restore issue' (both bound to '#', which is not in the supported punctuation set); 'Upload files' in the editor (official docs say Cmd+Shift+U, a third-party source says Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+A for 'attach image/file' -- genuinely conflicting on the key, so skipped); the documented alternate Italic binding Cmd/Ctrl+'>' ('>' is not in the supported punctuation set); Markdown-syntax formatting triggers (#, >, -, **, etc. typed at the start of a line) and heading shortcuts, which are in-field text-entry triggers, not fixed chords; positional 'go to team N' (Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+1-9) and 'set status N' (Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+1-9) shortcuts reported only by third-party cheat sheets with no official-docs corroboration; per-priority-level shortcuts (Shift+1-4/0) reported by only one, less reliable third-party source; mouse-only interactions (Shift+Click multi-select, drag-and-drop); and holding Shift while scrolling to pan the board horizontally (a held-modifier+scroll combination the grammar can't express). 'Copy issue as Markdown' is reached only via the command menu with no dedicated chord of its own, so it isn't listed separately from 'Open command menu'.",
  "actions": [
